assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor when searching products

Root cause: vendor version 2026-10-01 started splitting `/products` results into pages. It returns the first 5 items along with `next_cursor: "5"` and `total: 7`, but `search_products` only ever read the first response, so agents got 5 of 7 matches. The handler now keeps requesting `cursor=<next_cursor>` (a parameter the published spec already lists) until `next_cursor` is null, and returns all the items together. With 2026-01-01, `next_cursor` is always null, so the v1 fixtures send the same requests and give exactly the same output. Typecheck and lint pass, and so do all tests except the repro, which now fails with UNMATCHED_REQUEST because the recording has no `GET /products?q=cable&cursor=5`; it needs `fiks rerecord`. A second problem is still open and I left it alone because it wasn't the target: version 2026-10-01 also sends prices in cents (6900 instead of 69), so `items.price.range` is still violated.

Subject: follow next_cursor when searching products

